      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-t),\\,3,\\,\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2}⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,0).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $3$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14135210/assets/39266e152f7a52ee6cf56ad872704a110765e22c5d3fcea6f4b4c7565276ee24.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,0).$",
